00:19:16 said  No files have been changed yet. Here is the step 1 report. I'll wait for your OK before writing any code.
00:19:16 said  ## 1. Stack and where things live
00:19:16 said  **Stack:** It's a desktop app. A Python FastAPI server (`app/server/`) runs the engine (`src/audio_to_tab/`), and a Svelte 5 + TypeScript + Vite front end (`app/web/`) is shown in a pywebview window.
00:19:16 said  - **Generation pipeline**
00:19:16 said  - `src/audio_to_tab/pipeline.py` runs `run_pipeline` (load → separate → detect notes → tab → chords → lyrics → PDF). Lead/rhythm-split runs go through `_run_lead_rhythm_stage`.
00:19:16 said  - `app/server/jobs.py` runs each job in a background thread. Progress rows come from `src/audio_to_tab/progress_checklist.py`.
00:19:16 said  - `app/server/routes_jobs.py` handles `POST /api/jobs` and `GET /api/jobs/{id}`.
00:19:16 said  - Front end: `Entry.svelte` (upload, YouTube search, Convert) → `Waiting.svelte` (polls progress) → `Result.svelte`.
00:19:16 said  - **Tab data format**
00:19:16 said  - `TabDocument` → `TabEvent(start)` → `TabNote(start, end, string, fret, pitch)` in `src/audio_to_tab/tab_generate.py`. Times are in seconds.
00:19:16 said  - Each run saves a `result.json` with tempo, time signature, tuning, capo, and the detected beat and downbeat times. A real run in `data/ui_runs` has 158 beats and 42 downbeats.
00:19:16 said  - Lead/rhythm runs also save `lead_rhythm_notes.json`, which holds technique marks: slide, hammer-on, pull-off, palm mute and harmonic. It never holds bends or vibrato.
00:19:16 said  - **Tab viewer and player**
00:19:16 said  - `app/web/src/lib/screens/Result.svelte` holds the views, part switcher, a playhead on a fixed-size server SVG, click-to-seek, space to play, and auto-scroll.
00:19:16 said  - `app/web/src/lib/components/TabPlayer.svelte` is the transport (play/pause, seek bar, time).
00:19:16 said  - The SVG is built by `app/server/score.py` using `src/audio_to_tab/notation_view.py` (`tab_staff_svg`, `tab_playhead_layout`). Rhythm stems and beams come from `src/audio_to_tab/tab_rhythm.py`.
00:19:16 said  ## 2. Theme
00:19:16 said  - Everything is defined in `app/web/src/app.css` under `:root`:
00:19:16 said  - **Colours:** `--bg`, `--surface`, `--surface-2`, `--line`, `--text`, `--text-secondary`, `--muted`, `--accent`, `--accent-ink`, `--danger`, `--ok`, `--art`
00:19:16 said  - **Font sizes and line heights:** `--fs-1…6` / `--lh-1…6`
00:19:16 said  - **Spacing:** `--space-1…16`
00:19:16 said  - **Corners:** `--radius-1…3`
00:19:16 said  - **Fonts:** Satoshi (`--font-ui`, `--font-display`) and JetBrains Mono (`--font-mono`)
00:19:16 said  - **Motion:** `--motion`
00:19:16 said  - Components use these through `var(--…)` and `color-mix()` in scoped `<style>` blocks.
00:19:16 said  - The server SVG has its own ink colours (`#f4f7fb` and `#8fa0b5` in `notation_view.py`). The new viewer will use the CSS variables instead.
00:19:16 said  - `tests/test_web_tokens.py` checks several of these tokens and some `Result.svelte` details. I'll keep those passing.
00:19:16 said  ## 3. Gap analysis
00:19:16 said  | Feature | Status | Notes |
00:19:16 said  |---|---|---|
00:19:16 said  | Generate from upload or YouTube, then open viewer | **exists** | The button says "Convert". It opens the result when done. |
00:19:16 said  | Step-by-step progress | **exists** | Rows include Separating stems, Detecting notes and Mapping tablature. |
00:19:16 said  | AI-generated label | **missing** | |
00:19:16 said  | One track per stem | **partial** | A Lead / Rhythm / Combined switcher exists, but only for split runs. |
00:19:16 said  | Error message + retry, never hang silently | **partial** | An error bounces you back to the start with a banner. There's no retry and no warning if progress stalls. One failed poll also counts as a failed job. |
00:19:16 said  | 6-line tab in measures, with measure numbers | **exists** | It's a fixed-width server image. |
00:19:16 said  | Time signature and tempo on the tab | **missing** | Tempo only appears in the header line. |
00:19:16 said  | Tuning at the start | **exists** | |
00:19:16 said  | Rhythm (note durations) | **exists** | Stems, beams, flags and dots. |
00:19:16 said  | Technique marks | **partial** | Hammer-on, pull-off, slide and palm mute are saved for lead/rhythm runs but never drawn. Single-guitar runs have none. Bend and vibrato are **blocked**: the pipeline never produces them, and I won't invent them. |
00:19:16 said  | Wrapping layout that resizes, works on mobile | **missing** | Bars per line is fixed and the image just shrinks. |
00:19:16 said  | Track selector | **partial** | The part switcher. |
00:19:16 said  | Play/pause | **exists** | |
00:19:16 said  | Cursor that highlights the current note and auto-scrolls | **partial** | A line moves and rows scroll into view. There's no note or beat highlight. |
00:19:16 said  | Click a measure or note to jump | **partial** | Clicking anywhere on the tab works. Clicking a note doesn't. |
00:19:16 said  | Speed 25–100% without pitch change | **missing** | The browser audio can do this with no new library. |
00:19:16 said  | A/B loop | **missing** | |
00:19:16 said  | Metronome and count-in | **missing** | |
00:19:16 said  | Original audio vs synthesized tab audio | **missing** | Original and stem audio exist. There's no synth. |
00:19:16 said  | Per-track mute/solo | **missing** | |
00:19:16 said  | Keyboard shortcuts + help tooltip | **partial** | Only space. |
00:19:16 said  **Cursor sync:** notes sit at the times they were detected in the audio, and the cursor follows the audio's own clock, so drift can't build up over a song. Today the bar lines assume one fixed tempo. I'll place them on the beat and downbeat times already saved in `result.json`, so no storage change is needed. The metronome and count-in will click on those detected beats.
00:19:16 said  ## 4. Implementation plan
00:19:16 said  **No new dependencies.** The synth, metronome and count-in use the browser's built-in audio. Speed uses the audio player's built-in pitch-keeping.
00:19:16 said  1. **Structured tab data from the server.** `score.py` will also return a `tracks` list next to the current fields:
00:19:16 said  - notes, rhythm values and beam groups, reusing `tab_rhythm.py`
00:19:16 said  - technique marks from `lead_rhythm_notes.json`
00:19:16 said  - measures built from the saved downbeats, or a fixed tempo when none were detected
00:19:16 said  - the beat times, time signature, tempo, tuning, and an "AI-generated" flag
00:19:16 said  I'll also pass the saved beat grid to `tab_document_for` so the viewer matches the PDF. The Chords, Piano roll and Text views stay as they are.
00:19:16 said  - Edit `app/server/score.py`
00:19:16 said  - New test `tests/test_score_tracks.py`
00:19:16 said  2. **Generation flow.**
00:19:16 said  - The waiting screen gets a failure state with the message, the hint, **Try again** and **Back**.
00:19:16 said  - It will put up with brief connection errors instead of failing the job.
00:19:16 said  - It shows a "this is taking longer than usual" note with Retry/Back if progress stops updating.
00:19:16 said  - The server gets `POST /api/jobs/{id}/retry`, which reruns with the same audio and settings. The upload and YouTube code itself is untouched.
00:19:16 said  - Edit `app/server/jobs.py`, `app/server/routes_jobs.py`, `app/web/src/lib/screens/Waiting.svelte`, `app/web/src/App.svelte` (to pass the retried job id)
00:19:16 said  - Add a test to `tests/test_api_jobs.py`
00:19:16 said  3. **New tab viewer.**
00:19:16 said  - Measures wrap with the window width and work on phones.
00:19:16 said  - Tuning at the start of each line; time signature and tempo at the start.
00:19:16 said  - Measure numbers, rhythm above the tab, and technique marks (h, p, /, P.M.).
00:19:16 said  - Track selector, and an "AI-generated" label in the header.
00:19:16 said  - The Bars-per-line setting will only affect exports.
00:19:16 said  - New `app/web/src/lib/components/TabViewer.svelte`, new `app/web/src/lib/tabModel.ts` + `tabModel.test.ts` (converting between time and measure/beat)
00:19:16 said  - Edit `Result.svelte`
00:19:16 said  4. **Player basics.**
00:19:16 said  - Cursor plus highlight on the note being played, and auto-scroll.
00:19:16 said  - Click a note or measure to jump there.
00:19:16 said  - Speed 25/50/75/100%, kept at the same pitch.
00:19:16 said  - A/B loop: shift-click or drag across measures, then toggle the loop.
00:19:16 said  - Edit `TabPlayer.svelte`, `Result.svelte`, `tabModel.ts`
00:19:16 said  5. **Practice audio.**
00:19:16 said  - Synthesized playback of the tab using the browser's built-in audio (no library).
00:19:16 said  - A switch between original and synth, both following the same cursor.
00:19:16 said  - Metronome and count-in on the detected beats.
00:19:16 said  - Mute/solo per track.
00:19:16 said  - New `app/web/src/lib/synth.ts`
00:19:16 said  - Edit `TabPlayer.svelte`, `TabViewer.svelte`
00:19:16 said  6. **Shortcuts and final checks.**
00:19:16 said  - Shortcuts: Space play/pause, L loop, `[` and `]` set A/B at the cursor, − and = speed, M metronome, C count-in, with a small "?" tooltip listing them.
00:19:16 said  - Then run svelte-check, vitest, pytest and the front-end build. All are clean right now: 0 type errors, 21 front-end tests and 376 Python tests passing.
00:19:16 said  ## Questions before I start
00:19:16 said  1. The upload and YouTube screen button says **"Convert"**. Should I rename it to **"Generate tab"**? That touches the upload/YouTube screen, so I'll leave it unless you say yes.
00:19:16 said  2. Should YouTube search results get their own **"Generate tab"** button? Today you click Use, then Convert. Same reason: off unless you say yes.
00:19:16 said  3. Technique marks only exist for lead/rhythm-split runs. Should I run the pipeline's existing detection when a single-guitar tab is opened, or only show what was saved?
00:19:16 said  4. Bends and vibrato can't be shown because the pipeline never detects them. OK to leave those as blocked?
00:19:16 said  5. Mute/solo will control synth playback. The original recording is one mixed file, so a track can't be removed from it. Is that fine, or should soloing a track in original mode switch to that track's separated audio when it exists?
