09:43:26 said  I added a bar-by-bar role check to the lead + rhythm mode, based on the research. After the audio is split and turned into notes, it looks at each bar's playing (single notes or chords, whether the notes spell out a chord, whether the line moves smoothly, whether it repeats like a riff) and fixes what the audio split got wrong. It removes lead notes that leaked into the rhythm track, moves solos or fills from the rhythm track to the lead track when the lead is silent, and moves repeating chord-spelling riffs from the lead track to the rhythm track when the rhythm guitar is silent. Every move a…
09:43:26 said  All tests pass, including new ones for these cases, and the project check passes. The check is cautious: on your saved songs it would flag between none and 17 bars, and unclear bars are never moved.
09:43:26 said  It only runs when the Lead + Rhythm option is chosen, and I couldn't try it on a real lead/rhythm song because none are saved yet. Generating a song with Lead + Rhythm and comparing the two tabs is the next thing to try.
